  "status_text": "Picking one more pair on a ring comes with a checked price ceiling. Lean compared the cheapest way to pick a given number of pairs that share no corner with the cheapest way to pick one fewer (L-lib-1418). The ceiling uses the total price around the ring and the cheapest selection with one fewer pair. It becomes exact when every edge belongs to some cheapest larger selection. This supplies the next comparison for the search into weighted light schedules.",
